      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We are given that the line passes through the points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\). To find the equation of the line \\(y = ax + b\\), we need to determine the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).\n\nFirst, let's substitute the coordinates of the points into the equation \\(y = ax + b\\).\n\n1. Substitute \\((4,5)\\) into \\(y = ax + b\\):\n   \\[\n   5 = 4a + b\n   \\]\n\n2. Substitute \\((8,17)\\) into \\(y = ax + b\\):\n   \\[\n   17 = 8a + b\n   \\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n4a + b = 5 \\\\\n8a + b = 17\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), we can subtract the first equation from the second equation to eliminate \\(b\\):\n\\[\n(8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n8a + b - 4a - b = 12\n\\]\n\\[\n4a = 12\n\\]\n\\[\na = 3\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(a = 3\\), we can substitute this value back into the first equation to solve for \\(b\\):\n\\[\n4(3) + b = 5\n\\]\n\\[\n12 + b = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nb = 5 - 12\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -7\n\\]\n\nSo, the equation of the line is \\(y = 3x - 7\\). Therefore, \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = -7\\).\n\nFinally, we need to find \\(a - b\\):\n\\[\na - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
