      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The points $(4,5)$ and $(8,17)$ lie on the line given by the equation $y = ax + b$. Therefore, we can use the coordinates of these points to set up a system of linear equations to solve for $a$ and $b$, the slope and $y$-intercept of the line, respectively.\n\nFrom the given points, we have:\n\\[5 = 4a + b \\quad \\text{(1)}\\]\n\\[17 = 8a + b \\quad \\text{(2)}\\]\n\nTo eliminate $b$, we subtract equation (1) from equation (2):\n\\begin{align*}\n17 - 5 &= 8a - 4a + b - b \\\\\n12 &= 4a \\\\\na &= \\frac{12}{4} \\\\\na &= 3\n\\end{align*}\n\nSubstitute $a = 3$ into equation (1):\n\\begin{align*}\n5 &= 4(3) + b \\\\\n5 &= 12 + b \\\\\nb &= 5 - 12 \\\\\nb &= -7\n\\end{align*}\n\nThus, we have $a = 3$ and $b = -7$. Therefore, $a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = \\boxed{10}$. The answer is 10.",
