      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) for the line \\(y = ax + b\\) that passes through the points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\), we can use the point-slope form or substitute the points into the equation directly. Here, we will use substitution.\n\nFirst, substitute the point \\((4,5)\\) into the equation \\(y = ax + b\\):\n\\[5 = 4a + b.\\]\nThis gives us the first equation:\n\\[4a + b = 5. \\tag{1}\\]\n\nNext, substitute the point \\((8,17)\\) into the equation \\(y = ax + b\\):\n\\[17 = 8a + b.\\]\nThis gives us the second equation:\n\\[8a + b = 17. \\tag{2}\\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n4a + b = 5, \\\\\n8a + b = 17.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nTo eliminate \\(b\\), subtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[\n(8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5,\n\\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[\n4a = 12.\n\\]\nSolving for \\(a\\), we get:\n\\[\na = 3.\n\\]\n\nNow substitute \\(a = 3\\) back into the first equation:\n\\[\n4(3) + b = 5,\n\\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[\n12 + b = 5.\n\\]\nSolving for \\(b\\), we get:\n\\[\nb = 5 - 12 = -7.\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = -7\\), we can find \\(a - b\\):\n\\[\na - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(a - b\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
